---
mdv: "1.0"
title: Columns data
---

# Shipments by month

Values arrive one field at a time rather than one record at a time, so a
column is written once and read down instead of across. A flow sequence may
wrap onto the next line, and a block sequence says the same thing in the
form a hand-editing author usually reaches for.

The accepted grammar is MDV attribute notation, not YAML, and the whole of
the difference is visible here: `shipped` and `live` differ by one word each
and land on different types, because only `true` and `false` are booleans.
`no` is the string "no" — the Norway problem, declined.

```mdv bar
title: Units shipped by month
x: month
y: actual
format: columns
---
month:  [Jan, Feb,
         Mar]
actual: [120, 145, 132]
shipped: [yes, no, yes]
live:
  - true
  - false
  - true
```
